"""
Road grade under a planar frame: tan of the road angle along the frame's heading at its world
position, read without applying force or torque.

Ports: `frame_a` the point on the road and its heading, usually the chassis; `grade` the road
gradient tan(alpha) along the x axis of `frame_a`, positive uphill. It feeds the `grade` input of
`RoadLoad`.

`road` is a `Road.Slope`; build one from an OpenCRG height file with `Road.slope(file)`. The
default is the level road. Assumption: the grade is read at the frame's origin, not averaged over
the wheelbase.
"""
component RoadGrade
  "Point on the road and its heading"
  frame_a = Frame2D() {^frame_a}
  "Road gradient along the heading, tan(alpha)"
  grade = RealOutput() {^grade}
  "Road slope over world position and heading"
  structural parameter road::VehicleComponents.Road.Slope = VehicleComponents.Road.slope("dyad://VehicleComponents/data/roads/flat_z.crg")
relations
  grade = road(frame_a.x, frame_a.y, frame_a.phi)
  frame_a.fx = 0
  frame_a.fy = 0
  frame_a.tau = 0
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://VehicleComponents/Body/Planar/RoadGrade.svg"}},
  "_links": {
    "frame_a": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": -50, "y1": 450, "x2": 50, "y2": 550}}}},
    "grade": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 950, "y1": 450, "x2": 1050, "y2": 550}}}}
  }
}
end
